Track 1: Cardboard Refractors Chew the Sun
- Story & Context: When the wedding reception at the Van Buren boatyard descended into fistfights over dowry debts, bandleader Clara Bellini grabbed a plumber's wrench and hammered the venue's corrugated roof to establish an unyielding 7/8 mambo beat while her horn players dodged flying glass. The crowd halted when Hector dragged a massive scrap-copper refractor telescope to the gravel peak, aiming its lens straight into the blinding noon sky as the band slammed into their first synchronized industrial groove. Over the sound of squealing guitar feedback and clattering congas, Clara screamed into her ribbon mic, "Look through the chimney, darling, the brass is on fire!" sparking an ecstatic free-for-all dance that lasted until sunset.
