- Story & Context: Recorded in a single sweat-drenched take after midnight in an abandoned citrus cannery, this track captured Clara’s exhaustion and sudden realization that her family's circus dynasty was never coming back for her. Between soaring vibraphone cascades and crushing machine-stomp downbeats, the air smelled sharply of scorched paraffin wax, bruised key limes, and hot tube plates. Hector broke down mid-session, striking a loose engine block with a brass mallet while howling into the darkness, "You told me the glass would show us the stars, but all I see is salt water!"
