Track 3: The Van Buren Smelt-Pavilion
- Story & Context: Decades after the wedding brawl, local Sarasota teenagers turned the shuttered Van Buren foundry into an illicit roof-party haven, climbing rusted catwalks to trade pirate tape cassettes of the original bridal riot. The final track was recorded live among their descendants, where a thunderous choir of drop-hammer rhythms and shrieking baritone sax arpeggios shook the salt spray off the corrugated tin walls. An elder aerialist danced along the roof beam without a safety harness as the entire crowd roared the climactic refrain, "The circus died in the furnace, but the horn never cooled!"
